Like most multivariate outlier techniques, there is no direct information about the source of outlyingness for each observation. Therefore, we supplement the MCD with the corr-max transformation [33]. The corr-max transformation identifies a partition, W, that breaks the mMCD into a sum of p terms, where the combination of variables that contribute most to the sum are those that most influence the value of mMCD, i.e., \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
