Candès’ Robust Principal Component Analysis (RPCA) [32] aims to deconstruct a dataset X into two separate datasets, L and S, where X = L + S. Here L is a low-rank and robust approximation of X, and S is a generally sparse matrix with non-zero values representing deviations from the robust structure. L and S are determined by optimizing:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
